      "title": "Today, tomorrow, now",
      "goal": "Place things in time relative to now.",
      "notes": [
        "kallh means both \"yesterday\" and \"tomorrow\" — the verb tense tells you which. Punjabi treats \"the day next to today\" as one idea.",
        "savere, sham and raat are used with no preposition: main savere jaanda han — I go in the morning."
      ],
